mainmenu "SCI latency tester"

config SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	bool "Run as the SCI latency Central (else Peripheral)"
	help
	  When set, this build is the Central: it connects, drives the link to a
	  1.25 ms connection interval via the LE Connection Rate Update procedure,
	  sweeps the subrate factor and logs round-trip GATT latency over the VCOM
	  UART. When unset, this build is the Peripheral that advertises and accepts.

choice SCI_LATENCY_MODE
	prompt "Central test mode"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	default SCI_LATENCY_MODE_SWEEP
	help
	  Which measurement the Central runs after connecting and exchanging feature
	  page 1. Each mode is selected by stacking a mode .conf onto central.conf
	  (e.g. -DEXTRA_CONF_FILE="central.conf;mode_ecv_load.conf"). The default is
	  the RCV 1.25 ms + subrate-factor sweep.

config SCI_LATENCY_MODE_SWEEP
	bool "RCV 1.25 ms + subrate-factor sweep (default)"
	help
	  Drive the link to 1.25 ms via the Connection Rate Update procedure, then
	  sweep the subrate factor {1, 2, 4, 8} logging round-trip GATT latency. This
	  is the original tester behaviour (what plain central.conf builds).

config SCI_LATENCY_ECV_SWEEP
	bool "ECV: sweep the sub-1.25 ms band 1125..375 us (find the HW floor)"
	help
	  Instead of a fixed 1.25 ms interval + subrate sweep, start just below the
	  known-good RCV 1.25 ms and drive the link down the whole ECV (Extended
	  Connection Interval Values) band -- 1125, 1000, 875, 750, 625, 500, 375 us --
	  at subrate factor 1, measuring round-trip GATT latency at each and stopping at
	  the first interval the silicon cannot sustain. This finds the hardware floor
	  wherever it is: bsim (idealised radio) held 750/625 us, but real single-timer
	  silicon (cumulative drift + on-air margin at the standard 150 us tIFS) may
	  floor higher -- which the idealised bsim radio model cannot reproduce.

config SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_SUBRATE
	bool "Control: plain subrating at 7.5 ms (no SCI / Connection Rate Update)"
	help
	  Isolation control. Instead of the SCI Connection Rate Update to 1.25 ms,
	  the Central does a standard LE connection parameter update to a 7.5 ms
	  interval (BT_HCI_LE_INTERVAL_MIN, no SCI involved) and then sweeps the
	  subrate factor. This exercises only the original subrating path, so a clean
	  factor*interval result here vs a high floor on the 1.25 ms SCI build
	  pinpoints whether the latency is the SCI interaction or subrating itself.

config SCI_LATENCY_MODE_FSU_SWAP
	bool "FSU swap: negotiate 150->floor->150 us tIFS on a quiet link"
	help
	  Isolate the Frame Space Update inter-frame-space swap (Core 6.2 5.1.30.1)
	  from ECV interval timing. On a quiescent 7.5 ms link with no other traffic
	  in flight, negotiate FSU down from 150 us to the controller floor
	  (BT_CTLR_FSU_MIN_FRAME_SPACE_US), soak 30 s with 1 GATT read/s, then
	  negotiate back up to 150 us and soak 10 s more -- exercising the swap in
	  both directions. The naive apply has no transitional RX-window widening, so
	  the swap event may drop a packet on real radios; this mode is the first OTA
	  test of that. Verdict is PASS iff zero disconnects and zero read failures.

config SCI_LATENCY_MODE_ECV_LOAD
	bool "ECV load: stream the ZMK-split pointing load at an ECV interval"
	select BT_USER_PHY_UPDATE
	help
	  Drive the link to an ECV interval (SCI_LATENCY_ECV_INTERVAL_125US), request
	  2M PHY, optionally negotiate FSU (SCI_LATENCY_ECV_FSU, AFTER the conn-rate
	  change so the tIFS reset does not undo it), then have the peripheral stream
	  one 8-byte ZMK input-event notification per connection interval for
	  SCI_LATENCY_SOAK_SECONDS. The Central counts delivered vs OFFERED (a
	  tick-ceil of the generator period), sequence gaps, and -- if the controller
	  test hooks are enabled -- the connection-event count. Verdict is PASS iff
	  the link survived, delivered >= 90% of offered, and there were zero gaps.

endchoice

config SCI_LATENCY_ECV_INTERVAL_125US
	int "ECV load target connection interval (125 us units)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_MODE_ECV_LOAD
	default 6
	range 3 10
	help
	  Connection interval the ECV_LOAD mode drives the link to, in 125 us units:
	  6 = 750 us, 5 = 625 us, 4 = 500 us, 3 = 375 us. The controller must accept
	  it: the probe .conf opens the ECV floor via
	  CONFIG_BT_CTLR_SCI_ECV_INTERVAL_MIN_125US=3 (production default is 5/625 us).

config SCI_LATENCY_ECV_FSU
	bool "ECV load: negotiate FSU after the interval change"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_MODE_ECV_LOAD
	default y
	help
	  In the ECV_LOAD mode, after driving the link to the ECV interval, negotiate
	  a Frame Space Update down to the controller floor
	  (BT_CTLR_FSU_MIN_FRAME_SPACE_US, 80 us). The FSU must run AFTER the conn-rate
	  change: the conn-rate apply resets tIFS to the standard 150 us, so an earlier
	  FSU would be undone (ull_conn.c:2784). Set n for the airtime-vs-scheduler
	  control run (same load at the standard 150 us tIFS).

config SCI_LATENCY_SOAK_SECONDS
	int "ECV load soak duration (seconds)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_MODE_ECV_LOAD
	default 30
	help
	  How long the ECV_LOAD mode streams the ZMK-split pointing load and counts
	  delivered/offered/gaps. Interim RESULT lines are logged every 5 s.

config SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_INTERVAL_UNITS
	int "Plain-subrate connection interval (1.25 ms units)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_PLAIN_SUBRATE
	default 6
	help
	  Connection interval for the plain-subrate control, in 1.25 ms units.
	  6 = 7.5 ms (BT_HCI_LE_INTERVAL_MIN). 24 = 30 ms (matches the conn_subrate
	  bsim test's CONN_INTERVAL_UNITS, for an apples-to-apples HW-vs-bsim run).

config SCI_LATENCY_IDLE_GAP_MS
	int "Idle inter-read gap (ms)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	default 200
	help
	  Gap between isolated ("idle") reads. Must exceed the subrate skip period so
	  the peer re-sleeps between reads. bsim uses 400 ms.

config SCI_LATENCY_BURST_GAP_MS
	int "Burst inter-read gap (ms)"
	depends on SCI_LATENCY_CENTRAL
	default 2
	help
	  Gap between back-to-back ("burst") reads. Must stay inside the continuation
	  (awake) window = (factor-1) * interval, so the gap has to scale with the
	  interval: ~2 ms at 1.25 ms, 50 ms at 30 ms (bsim's value).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
